From 32eb831dd7900e8edf8d1b10b76b4e4fc1f8bc6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 02:51:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Keep the screensaver down across a long-press exit and
 page reloads

Reopening the app after a long-press exit flashed the screensaver before
the wake: the machine confirmed the sleep while the app was leaving, and
that overlay was the first frame shown on return. The screensaver and
panel dim are now suppressed from the exit until the return.

The exit marker moves to localStorage. Decaid unloads the page after ten
minutes in the background and reloads it on return, which lost the
in-memory marker, so a long absence got the screensaver instead of a
wake. A page loaded with the marker set is itself the return.

If the app is still on screen when the check runs (iOS, or a failed
exit), the suppression is undone and the overlay follows the machine.

